1
00:00:00,140 --> 00:00:02,700
Before your test, stop rereading.

2
00:00:02,940 --> 00:00:05,680
Only 2 of 10 study methods rated high.

3
00:00:05,960 --> 00:00:06,640
Which two?

4
00:00:06,940 --> 00:00:09,960
In 2013, researchers reviewed 10 popular

5
00:00:09,980 --> 00:00:10,960
ways to study.

6
00:00:11,220 --> 00:00:13,440
Rereading, highlighting, and summarizing

7
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:14,680
all rated low.

8
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,040
Rereading feels easy because the words

9
00:00:17,060 --> 00:00:17,900
look familiar.

10
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:19,980
On test day, the page is gone,

11
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,560
and you have to pull it from memory.

12
00:00:21,840 --> 00:00:24,380
The first high method is practice testing.

13
00:00:24,580 --> 00:00:25,540
Close your notes.

14
00:00:25,680 --> 00:00:27,320
Write down everything you remember

15
00:00:27,340 --> 00:00:28,560
about one topic.

16
00:00:28,760 --> 00:00:30,800
Then open them and check what you missed.

17
00:00:31,020 --> 00:00:32,600
The second is spacing.

18
00:00:32,880 --> 00:00:35,160
Study the same topic on different days

19
00:00:35,180 --> 00:00:36,480
instead of all at once.

20
00:00:36,680 --> 00:00:38,180
It gets its own video soon.

21
00:00:38,360 --> 00:00:39,660
Try the first one tonight.

22
00:00:40,300 --> 00:00:42,020
Save this for your next test.
